      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Rock of Ages” (a/k/a, “Hanukkah-Hymn”) was written by the prominent Reform movement rabbi Gustav Gottheil, and composed in English verse to be sung to a popular melody for the piyyut Maoz Tsur. It was first published in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Jewish Chronicle</tei:hi>, No1341 (new series), 21 December 1894, p. 18. The work cannot be regarded as a translation, or even a free translation or paraphrasic translation, but rather as a song inspired by the initial lines of the first and last stanzas of Maoz Tsur. Three of the five stanzas were published as “Hanukkah-Hymn” in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Union Prayerbook</tei:hi> (1895), p. 46.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_66452_notes"/>
